 up with a bunch of empty tasks). The in-page logic (the WebContentsObserver…"],["aa23ff91_1b531052",39,-1,1,"instead of removing private i think we should move under AssociateWebContentsToTask"],["e17b9c99_d93c13a5",27,-1,0,"this boolean seems to control the sidepanel visibility indirectly, but is not neccessarily if the sidepanel is open or not, its basically whether the sidepanel should be open or not on the next…"],["ea3558b4_9aa8d896",23,-1,1,"be careful with optional bool, it can have different semantics for truthyness than a regular pointer. my recommendation is to just return false if theres no task or CHECK, instead of using optional."],["759bf44b_a7d88a15",23,0,1,"I assumed we'd use `ContextualTasksService::GetTaskById(...)` and store this flag in the `ContextualTask` itself. Is the reason why we have it here because we need a synchronous API? See this bug:…"]],0,511],[7131608,20403,28,0.737,0.556,[[0,257]],[],0,512],[7139764,20404,68,2.361,1.866,[[19,5]],[["ef73c94f_e8e8ba84",27,-1,1,"open or not should be associated with tab, you can have a tab opening a WebContents, while another tab close on the same WebContents due to experiments. I think there are 2 options to do this: 1.…"]],0,514],[7145777,20405,29,0.737,0.556,[[19,6]],[],0,515],[7152324,20406,75,2.361,1.866,[[19,0.695,7,55],[0,0.305,260,20]],[["9533e745_d4a2956c",38,0,1,"add the context in DetachWebContentsAtForInsertion instead of renaming"]],0,517],[7153738,20406,21,0.737,0.556,[[19,8]],[],0,518],[7157911,20407,28,0.737,0.556,[[19,9]],[],0,519],[7165629,20411,150,4.21,3.407,[[19,10]],[["35e0415f_e647b216",23,0,0,"Out of curiosity, what is blocking us from moving back to a map? I feel like it would be easier to write the logic to support this."],["390cc536_ea6ec5e5",27,0,1,"Please fix this WARNING reported by Spellchecker: \"exisiting\" is a possible misspelling of \"existing\". To bypass Spellchecker, ad... \"exisiting\" is a possible misspelling of \"existing\". To bypass…"],["7098d8fe_495613ae",23,0,0,"This is a bit scary to read through - if we hit this case second, isn't it possible we've got two entries with the same ID in the list?"],["cdaf8a77_22b41464",40,0,1,"nit: Remove duplicate"]],0,520],[7173736,20412,139,4.21,3.407,[[19,11]],[["1099eb12_9c274c6f",23,0,1,"nit: early return here to reduce indentations below: if (!cached_item) { return; }"]],0,521],[7173798,20417,159,4.21,3.407,[[19,12]],[["292098aa_1b052d7f",23,-4,1,"has this been tested with the tab->panel transition? it will also call \"detach \" which will fire this kRemoved event"],["704adda3_a39f0efc",23,-4,1,"instead lets use a TabIterator, and then get the contents from the Tab."],["851d6de4_97b4f7e3",23,-4,1,"lets listen for \"kReplaced\" as well since we are storing session id i dont know if session id changes on discard."]],0,522],[7202525,20418,52,1.341,1.058,[[19,13]],[["56aa0798_384efa05",23,-1,1,"what is the implication of this CL if the new tab is opened by clicking a link in the side panel? I think the side panel link click has a special navigation interception and will associate the tab Id…"],["ecbdeeba_296a1ace",23,-1,1,"Does this happen before we switch to the new tab?"]],0,523],[7207503,20419,213,4.21,3.407,[[19,0.922,14,197],[8,0.078,36,16]],[["4dadf00c_f4ab68cc",23,-1,1,"nit: ShouldBeOpen?"],["e39b9720_f9bf2341",27,-1,1,"nit: ```suggestion void UpdateOpenState(bool is_open); ```"]],0,524],[7248633,20433,322,7.601,6.192,[[19,15]],[],0,525],[7251784,20433,16,0.737,0.556,[[19,16]],[["b83a6982_ec5c5d71",23,0,0,"We call browser_window_->GetActiveTabInterface() to get the current tab here https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/browser/contextual_tasks/contextual_tasks_side_panel_coordi…"]],0,526],[7253629,20433,4,0.259,0.185,[[24,5]],[],0,527],[7254332,20434,34,1.341,1.058,[[19,17]],[],0,528],[7257495,20437,41,1.341,1.058,[[19,18]],[["1ffc0ba3_5d2a6b03",36,0,0,"I think this patch also addresses 467756141, can you add it to the list if so?"],["7b8f8a45_e0